        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "917351fb-d53b-5ae3-a058-9fc912956acc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Game of Life, The Checkered Game of Life, History of the World, Be a Broadway Star\n- People: Milton Bradley, Ragnar Brothers\n- Concepts: player counts, gameplay mechanics, publication dates, epochs, empires\n\nFacts:\n- Milton Bradley originally created The Game of Life in 1860 as The Checkered Game of Life.\n- History of the World was originally published in 1991 and was designed by Ragnar Brothers.\n- The Game of Life is also known simply as Life.\n- Variations of The Game of Life accommodate eight to ten players.\n- History of the World is played by up to six players across seven epochs, and each player controls a different empire in each epoch.\n- Be a Broadway Star uses a game board similar to The Game of Life, and players move according to two rolled dice.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5a389b4d-4f16-5329-8a99-e8c0b45a5508",
        "text": "Page: The Game of Life. Sentence: The Game of Life, also known simply as Life, is a board game originally created in 1860 by Milton Bradley, as The Checkered Game of Life.\nPage: The Game of Life. Sentence: Variations of the game accommodate eight to ten players.\nPage: History of the World (board game). Sentence: History of the World (often abbreviated HotW) is a board game designed by Ragnar Brothers and originally published in 1991.\nPage: History of the World (board game). Sentence: It is played by up to six different players in seven different epochs; each player playing a different empire in each epoch.\nPage: Be a Broadway Star. Sentence: Players move around a game board similar to The Game of Life, with movement determined by two rolled dice.",
